  "scope": "Phase-three Level, Hierarchy and Attribute views: workspace instances, read-only scene projections, registered edits, parameter inputs and object picking. No SDK or viewport transfer changes.",
  "status": "This view migration batch is complete. Resource browsers and default contributions remain in phase three; completed_phase stays 2.",
  "implemented": [
    "Level/Hierarchy share a pointer-free tree view; Attribute manager/chooser share a catalog projection and registered commands. Each workspace instance owns its selection, filter, expansion and input.",
    "Workspace roles, pinned primary windows, default docking, focus, lifetime, instance inspection and picking replace host managers, display flags and title routing. Cached pure views remain usable during native work; native commands stay excluded.",
    "SceneCommands owns the published scene version, bounded native tree cache and document Worksets. Changes reuse core edits; clipboard ownership and history behavior are retained.",
    "Parameter values and copy/delete dependency options reuse ParameterBox through a registered overlay. Failed input preparation preserves existing input. Closed/stale targets cannot write a reused object.",
    "Drag records carry object lifetimes and attribute catalog versions. New and legacy consumers resolve them at dispatch. Picking supports modal parameter editors and consumes empty view regions.",
    "A prepared document establishes the receiving history save point. Undo after open/new restores clean state; modified/imported candidates remain modified.",
    "Removed LevelManager, HierarchyManager and ManagerWindows implementations; moved clipboard definitions into core. Dependency checks reject indirect native/state access from pure scene views.",
    "An independent module navigates actual scene instances, reads their selection through C callbacks and submits the same visibility command. Regressions cover independent Level/Hierarchy/Attribute instances, closed scopes, undo, catalog reuse and native work."
  ],
